WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.570
Listen to the letter c
in two Spanish words.

2
00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:04.580
casa.

3
00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:05.590
cena.

4
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.290
Now the letter g.

5
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.490
gato.

6
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.330
gente.

7
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.030
Same letter on the page.

8
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.110
A different sound in your ear.

9
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.630
So what decides which sound the
letter c or the letter g makes?

10
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.290
In this mission, you'll hear
the five short, pure vowels,

11
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.900
and meet a letter
that's always silent.

12
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.790
You'll learn how to keep the
letter c and the letter g hard,

13
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.070
and how the n with a
tilde sounds in España.

14
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.790
Then you'll hear the tap and
the roll that split two words:

15
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.510
pero, perro.

16
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.230
Your mission: crack the rules
that turn Spanish letters into

17
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.490
sounds.
